<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Gulf basis bids weaken.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Gulf basis bids weaken.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were weaker Wednesday at the Gulf of Mexico, grain dealers in the U.S. High Plains said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, dealers said light to moderate snow was forecast to fall Wednesday night and Thursday across Oklahoma and southern and western Kansas.</p>
<p>&quot;They're calling for three to six inches here in Enid,&quot; an Oklahoma dealer said. &quot;As much as I hate the snow, we need the moisture bad.&quot;</p>
<p>Dealers said farmer sales of wheat had been extremely slow Tuesday.  </p>
